{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"RLSA-2026:98593","published":"2026-11-13T12:06:37.188502Z","modified":"2026-11-13T12:45:09.143116383Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-33818","CVE-2026-56853","CVE-2026-56862","CVE-2026-78669","CVE-2026-97031"],"summary":"Important: go-fdo-server security update","details":"This package provides a server-side implementation of the FIDO Device Onboard (FDO) specification, written in Go. FDO is an open standard for the late binding of device credentials, allowing for automated and secure on-boarding of devices when they are first powered on in their final location.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* encoding/asn1: golang: Go encoding/asn1: Denial of Service via excessive recursion in Unmarshal (CVE-2026-33818)\n\n* net/http: golang: Go net/http: Unencrypted HTTP/2 connections vulnerable to Denial of Service (CVE-2026-56853)\n\n* crypto/tls: golang: Golang crypto/tls: Denial of Service via indefinite KeyUpdate messages (CVE-2026-56862)\n\n* crypto/tls: golang: crypto/tls: Denial of Service via multiple ECH outer extension references (CVE-2026-97031)\n\n* net/http: net/http/internal/http2: golang.org/x/net/http2: net/http: Denial of Service via excessive HTTP/2 SETTINGS frames (CVE-2026-78669)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"go-fdo-server-debugsource","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/go-fdo-server-debugsource?distro=rocky-linux-10&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:1.0.1-6.el10_3.9"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"AppStream"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:98593.json"}},{"package":{"name":"go-fdo-server","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/go-fdo-server?distro=rocky-linux-10&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM"